      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Cloud KMS Integration**\n\nOkay, I've decided to use Google Cloud KMS as the managed key service for envelope encryption. The next step is fleshing out the `envelope_encrypt.py` code structure, making sure that it clearly reflects the chosen KMS provider within its core logic and configuration. The focus is now on implementing the KMS interaction.\n\n\n**Implementing KMS Integration**\n\nI'm now fully committed to Google Cloud KMS. I'm starting the `envelope_encrypt.py` file, focusing on integrating the KMS client for both encryption and decryption. I'll need to define functions to handle KMS key interactions, including encrypting and decrypting data encryption keys. The functions will take plaintext, the KMS key path, and the ciphertext as input, handling KMS client usage.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789859922893,
          "start": 1789859919240
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bbf6f588001CLmvYJfLdOG7US",
